sit":"Spot check","type_raw":"Spot Check","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8371&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=370541&INSPECTION_NN=370541","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"356141","date":"2020-01-29","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":2,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8371&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=356141&INSPECTION_NN=356141","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":43,"title":"In-use utensils: properly stored","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"3-304.12","citation_text":"3-304.12  (C) In-Use Utensils are stored incorrectly at the salad bar. Observed children to use tongs and then throw them back into the food so that the cut peppers and broccoli are contaminated by the handles. Store in-use utensils: 1) in the food with the handle above the top of the food item; 2) on a clean and sanitized surface; 3) in running water; 4) in a container of hot water maintained at or above 135 °F. Reference 3-304.12. Suggest providing holders for the tongs or develop some system of use so that the food is not contaminated. The kindergarden class is throwing the tongs in to the food. They may be too young to serve themselves."},{"item":44,"title":"Utensils, equipment & linens: properly stored, dried, & handled","repeat":false,"comment":"4-903.11(A), (B) and (D)  (C) Clean Equipment/Utensils/Linens/Single-Use Articles stored incorrectly. Observed plates on the cart to be stored with the food contact surface exposed. Children were putting their hands on plates that were not their own on the food contact surface. Equipment, Utensils, Linens and Single-Use Articles shall be stored: 1) in a clean and dry location; 2) away or protected from contamination; 3) at least six inches above the floor; 4) covered or inverted. Reference 4-903.11(A), (B) and (D). Invert plates, instruct children to only take the top plate, and touch only the plate they are going to eat from.","citation":"","citation_text":""}]},{"id":"331550","date":"2019-05-14","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8371&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=331550&INSPECTION_NN=331550","fetched":true,"findings":[]},{"id":"323537","date":"2019-02-14","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":2,"label":"Minor issues","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl/ESTABLISHMENT/ShowViolationTablePage.aspx?ESTABLISHMENT=8371&ESTTST_CTY=sJRNEgWYzzs%3d&VIOLATION_INSPECTION=323537&INSPECTION_NN=323537","fetched":true,"findings":[{"item":47,"title":"Food and non-food contact surfaces cleanable, properly designed, constructed, and used","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"4-202.11","citation_text":"4-202.11  (Pf) Food-Contact surface of the measuring cup for popcorn oil is no longer smooth and easily cleansable. A food-contact surface that is not smooth and easily cleansable can harbor bacteria that con be transfer to food. Replace with a National Sanitation Foundation/ANSI approved surface. Reference 4-202.11."},{"item":49,"title":"Non-food contact surfaces clean","repeat":false,"comment":"","citation":"4-602.13","citation_text":"4-602.13  (C) Soil residue present on the floor under the sink at baseboard heaters. Baseboard heaters are also soiled. Two different types of cockroaches are observed on the glue board in this area. Clean all non-food contact surfaces frequently to prevent soil accumulation.  Reference 4-602.13."}]},{"id":"274912","date":"2018-05-14","visit":"Routine","type_raw":"Original","risk":0,"repeat":0,"grp":0,"label":"No issues written up","detail_url":"https://public.cdpehs.com/ILEnvPbl